# Phase 006 Group 05 — transformation reconciliation guardrails

Status: **Accepted — HLTH-041–HLTH-054; H05-01–H05-44 pass. Group 06 has consumed these semantics; Group 07 is next.**

Preserve permanently:

- local Observation ≠ downstream-relevant upstream context ≠ derived reconciliation Observation ≠ reconciliation Assessment;
- Lineage relationship ≠ reconciliation formula ≠ status propagation ≠ causality;
- every reconciliation binds exact transformation/version, input/output identities and roles, fields/keys/measures, grain/population/window and material cycle/version context;
- A+B→C never implies generic row-count arithmetic;
- joins use eligible populations, directional match/unmatched rates, key/cardinality and fan-out semantics;
- many-to-many amplification can be legitimate; duplicate keys can amplify without missing input rows;
- filter conservation applies only under exact pure-filter semantics; selection can change downstream distributions/DQ measures;
- aggregation conservation is measure-specific; averages, ratios, percentages, quantiles and distinct counts are not generically composable;
- dedupe binds duplicate equivalence and survivor selection; output uniqueness does not rewrite source uniqueness;
- bag union is additive only under explicit conditions; DISTINCT union/merge/upsert require overlap/action semantics;
- downstream null/completeness is not inherited; joins, filters, defaults, casts and derivations can introduce/remove/replace value states;
- output success/completion does not prove all required inputs current; bind consumed versions and permitted cadence/lag;
- distribution/quantile/normalization relationships require semantics that preserve meaning;
- derived reconciliation retains source provenance, availability, coverage, approximation/uncertainty, restriction and temporal limitations;
- derivation/aggregation is not declassification;
- multi-hop reconciliation requires explicit valid composition; do not infer A↔C conservation from A↔B and B↔C alone;
- asset-level Lineage does not make unused fields/partitions/populations relevant;
- upstream `warning`, `violates`, Baseline atypicality, severity or waiver never recursively propagates downstream;
- upstream violation can coexist with downstream meets; upstream meets can coexist with downstream violation;
- reconciliation mismatch or first localization is not root cause;
- causal propositions remain Causal Claim under REF-013–REF-020;
- historical reconciliation uses then-effective Lineage/transformation/reconciliation/input/output versions and preserves reassessment history.

Accepted Group 06 composes reconciliation Assessments only as explicit profile components. It does not convert reconciliation success into overall health, readiness, gate state, or causality. Result freshness/current-cycle alignment and exact-use suitability remain independently evaluated.

Group 07 must verify these relationships survive full Phase 006 consolidation without blind propagation or summary flattening.

Do not select Spark/SQL implementation, DQX/Metric Views realization, graph/storage design, scheduler/control topology, or streaming/caching architecture from these semantics.